# Three players: a bound checked from the table to the limit

A symmetric table on six hats for three players, found by a search on
2026-11-28 (`research/hats/players/results/t6-73226.txt`).  Lean's kernel
counts its wins, `73226` out of `262144` (`wins3_six`), and the theorem on
repeated resets gives the limit `73225 / 261950 = 0.279538...`
(`tendsto_six`), above the `9119 / 32670 = 0.279124...` of Buhler,
Freiling, Graham, Kariv, Roche, Tiefenbruck, Van Alten and Yeroshkin
(`six_gt`).

So the best win rate for three players is at least `73225 / 261950`, with
nothing left to a program.  (A table on seven hats gives a little more,
`6817 / 24381`, counted by programs.)
-/

